WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:26.910
<v Speaker 1>Audubillahi mina Shaytan regime Bismillahu Rahmanur Rahim Allahumma saliya ala Sayyidina Muhammadin Wa ala Ali Sayyidina Muhammadin kamasalayta wa salamta wa barakta wa rahimta wa tarahamta ala Ibrahim Wa ala Ali Ibrahim fil alamina Inna Kahmidu Majid Rabbish Rahli Sadri wa yaserli Amri Wahlul Uqtata millisani of Kahukawli Assalamu alaikum wa rahmatullahi wa barakatu

2
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:48.590
<v Speaker 1>Now that we understand these meanings of Rab and Rahman and Raheem, now that we understand these terms, I want to share with you a beautiful spiritual representation that Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala has created for us through the example of the womb, the Rahem.

3
00:00:50.510 --> 00:00:57.710
<v Speaker 1>To quickly reiterate these terms, Rab is a combination of six things in classical Arabic.

4
00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:25.710
<v Speaker 1>The definition is a Rabbuhu al-Maliku was Sayyidu al-Murabbi al-Murshid wal-Muna'im al-Qayyim So a Rab is an owner and he is the one with complete authority over its property He is the one who nurtures his creation guides it benefits it by bestowing generous and undeserving gifts upon it and he is the one who maintains it

5
00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:31.230
<v Speaker 1>So this is who Allah is, right?

6
00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:35.550
<v Speaker 1>That's His primary role with His creation of Rabb.

7
00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:43.310
<v Speaker 1>And all His other attributes, they basically center around and they stem from His Rabul biyya.

8
00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.990
<v Speaker 1>So if someone asks, who is Allah?

9
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.310
<v Speaker 1>The answer to that question is Allah is Rabb.

10
00:01:52.990 --> 00:01:55.150
<v Speaker 1>Now, as for His nature,

11
00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:59.070
<v Speaker 1>His nature is Ar-Rahman and Ar-Raheem.

12
00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:12.510
<v Speaker 1>So the manner in which he executes or the way he carries out the functions of his Rubul biyya, it is through intense and consistent love, compassion and mercy.

13
00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:23.790
<v Speaker 1>So now that we understand these concepts, I want to share this example that Allah has created for us through the womb.

14
00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:32.270
<v Speaker 1>You know, by studying the womb, we can actually understand a lot about our master's plan for us.

15
00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:36.430
<v Speaker 1>Just by studying the relationship of the womb with its fetus.

16
00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:43.390
<v Speaker 1>Because this womb, it is the first rub of the fetus.

17
00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:51.390
<v Speaker 1>And it demonstrates the exact same principles of Rahmaniyya and Rahimiyya in its interaction with it.

18
00:02:52.190 --> 00:03:05.150
<v Speaker 1>This is why there is a Hadith in which Rasulullah , he said This world is a womb for the afterlife.

19
00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:20.670
<v Speaker 1>In other words, the story of our lives in this world, it tells a tale about the kind of life that we're going to have in the afterlife because

20
00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:30.910
<v Speaker 1>This world, this dunya that we're living in is the womb or access the womb and we are the fetus in that womb.

21
00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:43.230
<v Speaker 1>And just as the brief and temporary residence in a womb is actually preparation for this worldly life,

22
00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:51.470
<v Speaker 1>Our stay in this temporal world is nothing more than a short duration of preparation for the afterlife.

23
00:03:54.030 --> 00:04:02.030
<v Speaker 1>Now, if you look at the Rahem, the womb, you'll see all six principles of Rubbiya at work.

24
00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:08.110
<v Speaker 1>It has ownership and it has authority over the embryo, right?

25
00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:13.870
<v Speaker 1>It nurtures the embryo, it helps the embryo grow and develop into a fetus.

26
00:04:14.590 --> 00:04:19.790
<v Speaker 1>So the womb is Malik, it is Sayyid and it is Murabbi.

27
00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:37.150
<v Speaker 1>Then we see that the womb, it bestows these priceless gifts upon the fetus to the development of its eyes, its nose, its ears, hands, feet, the heart, the intellect and all of its internal and external organs.

28
00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:42.670
<v Speaker 1>So we can see that the womb is also the Muna'im, the bestower of gifts.

29
00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:52.590
<v Speaker 1>We also know that the womb, it manages the entire development process of the embryo from its conception all the way until it is fully developed.

30
00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:55.550
<v Speaker 1>So the womb is also ayam.

31
00:04:57.390 --> 00:05:05.710
<v Speaker 1>So we can see that the womb, it actually acts as the very first physical rub that we come in contact with.

32
00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:12.670
<v Speaker 1>And this very first act, it actually demonstrates the design

33
00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:16.510
<v Speaker 1>of how Allah created this mechanism.

34
00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:26.350
<v Speaker 1>It demonstrates the act of Rububiyya by carrying out all six functions of the definition of the word Rab, right?

35
00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:29.230
<v Speaker 1>Malik, Sayyid, Murabbi, Murshid, Munhayim, Qayyim.

36
00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:36.510
<v Speaker 1>Now, what happens once the baby is delivered into this world?

37
00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:40.830
<v Speaker 1>Who is the baby handed over to?

38
00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:48.750
<v Speaker 1>It is handed over to its loving mother who becomes the next immediate Rabb of that baby.

39
00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:51.390
<v Speaker 1>Not the father, the mother.

40
00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:54.910
<v Speaker 1>It's the mother that becomes the next Rabb.

41
00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:56.350
<v Speaker 1>Why?

42
00:05:56.590 --> 00:05:58.270
<v Speaker 1>Because she feeds it.

43
00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:00.830
<v Speaker 1>She takes care of it.

44
00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:04.350
<v Speaker 1>There is this transference of Rubbiya that takes place.

45
00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:07.550
<v Speaker 1>The mother now takes ownership of the baby.

46
00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:10.110
<v Speaker 1>The mother now takes authority over it.

47
00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:22.990
<v Speaker 1>The mother assumes the responsibility of nurturing it, helping it grow and develop, teaching it, guiding it, setting it to purpose, showering all these gifts and blessings upon it.

48
00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:32.510
<v Speaker 1>She becomes the one who maintains that baby's sustenance in all its various forms, physical, emotional, psychological.

49
00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.390
<v Speaker 1>So we can see that our mothers become the next immediate Arab

50
00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:43.070
<v Speaker 1>Right after the Rububiya of the womb, the Raham, it's completed.

51
00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:49.630
<v Speaker 1>Now father is also a Rab, but his Rububiya gets executed through the mother.

52
00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:55.710
<v Speaker 1>You see, the father always uses the mother as a means for her.

53
00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:59.950
<v Speaker 1>He facilitates her functions of Rububiya.

54
00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:05.150
<v Speaker 1>That's the role of the father, but the primary caretaker of the child is always the mother.

55
00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:13.710
<v Speaker 1>So now let's study this Hadith to better understand the underlying principles that are at work.

56
00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:19.190
<v Speaker 1>So Rasulullah , he said, .

57
00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:24.270
<v Speaker 1>This temporal world is the womb of the afterlife.

58
00:07:26.030 --> 00:07:29.870
<v Speaker 1>So let's examine the fetus and the womb of its mother.

59
00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:34.830
<v Speaker 1>Is it the womb actually doing all the work?

60
00:07:35.310 --> 00:07:44.670
<v Speaker 1>Or is it the mother doing all the work behind the scenes and letting this womb act as an intermediary between herself and her child?

61
00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:47.790
<v Speaker 1>Is it the womb or the mother?

62
00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:52.110
<v Speaker 1>We know it's always the mother, right?

63
00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:54.830
<v Speaker 1>The mother is the one taking care of the baby's needs.

64
00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:58.750
<v Speaker 1>She is the one eating all the right things.

65
00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:02.990
<v Speaker 1>She is making sure she doesn't bump into things so that her baby doesn't get hurt.

66
00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:11.710
<v Speaker 1>She's the one getting all the ultrasounds done, taking all those painful but necessary blood tests, all those injections.

67
00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:15.230
<v Speaker 1>So she is the one actually suffering for the baby.

68
00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:20.990
<v Speaker 1>Baby is living comfortably in the womb, but it's the mother doing all the work, right?

69
00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:24.510
<v Speaker 1>The mother is the one doing all the hard work all along.

70
00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:30.910
<v Speaker 1>But from the perspective of the fetus, who is doing all the work?

71
00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:34.430
<v Speaker 1>The womb, not the mother.

72
00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:39.870
<v Speaker 1>You see, the fetus has absolutely no knowledge of its mother.

73
00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:46.110
<v Speaker 1>All it knows, all it recognizes, all it understands is the womb.

74
00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:51.550
<v Speaker 1>If I ask the fetus, who do you think is feeding you?

75
00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:56.030
<v Speaker 1>Who do you think is nurturing you, taking care of you, sustaining you?

76
00:08:56.510 --> 00:09:00.910
<v Speaker 1>Who is doing all the work that is necessary for your health and development?

77
00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.310
<v Speaker 1>What will the fetus reply?

78
00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:05.390
<v Speaker 1>The womb.

79
00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:13.390
<v Speaker 1>The fetus has absolutely no knowledge of the existence of its mother.

80
00:09:14.190 --> 00:09:14.750
<v Speaker 1>You see?

81
00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:16.030
<v Speaker 1>What mother?

82
00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:17.630
<v Speaker 1>Where's the mother?

83
00:09:17.630 --> 00:09:18.590
<v Speaker 1>I don't see a mother.

84
00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:20.750
<v Speaker 1>All I see is the womb.

85
00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:22.030
<v Speaker 1>There is no mother.

86
00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:23.310
<v Speaker 1>It's just cause and effect.

87
00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:30.190
<v Speaker 1>When I tell this fetus, no, no, it's not the womb, it's the mother.

88
00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:31.630
<v Speaker 1>She is the one feeding you.

89
00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:33.790
<v Speaker 1>She's the one taking care of you.

90
00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:37.070
<v Speaker 1>This womb is only an intermediary.

91
00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:38.190
<v Speaker 1>It's a means.

92
00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.510
<v Speaker 1>And the fetus says, you know, what are you talking about?

93
00:09:41.510 --> 00:09:43.550
<v Speaker 1>It's the umbilical cord that's feeding me.

94
00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:48.590
<v Speaker 1>That's what gets me this blood that is carrying all the nutrients.

95
00:09:48.590 --> 00:09:51.790
<v Speaker 1>I get fed by that, the umbilical cord.

96
00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:55.390
<v Speaker 1>The umbilical cord is responsible for my development.

97
00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:56.270
<v Speaker 1>There is no mother.

98
00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:01.070
<v Speaker 1>And so I explain, no, no, there is a mother.

99
00:10:01.550 --> 00:10:03.150
<v Speaker 1>She is all around you.

100
00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:10.030
<v Speaker 1>You are within the love, the care, the concern, and the mercy of your mother.

101
00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:14.030
<v Speaker 1>This womb wouldn't exist if she didn't exist.

102
00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:17.950
<v Speaker 1>And this womb that you're in, it's actually temporary.

103
00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:20.510
<v Speaker 1>This is not the world you were created for.

104
00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:26.910
<v Speaker 1>Believe me, this world is filthy, it is dark, it is immensely constricted.

105
00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:34.590
<v Speaker 1>There is an amazing and a beautiful world that exists outside this womb that has been created just for you.

106
00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:42.270
<v Speaker 1>And that world is so magnificent that you cannot even imagine its glory right now within this womb.

107
00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:46.310
<v Speaker 1>Trust me, this womb is filth compared to that world.

108
00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:55.150
<v Speaker 1>So if you think this womb is kind and merciful to you, let me tell you, it doesn't even compare to the love and the mercy of your mother.

109
00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:59.710
<v Speaker 1>Because your mother is going to take care of you in the next world.

110
00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:06.750
<v Speaker 1>She will shower you with so much love that you have absolutely no idea.

111
00:11:06.830 --> 00:11:08.910
<v Speaker 1>You cannot even imagine that while you're in this womb.

112
00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:13.630
<v Speaker 1>But the fetus says, what are you talking about?

113
00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:16.830
<v Speaker 1>I am really really happy here.

114
00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:22.350
<v Speaker 1>Everything I need is being taken care of for me right here.

115
00:11:23.950 --> 00:11:25.870
<v Speaker 1>Why do I need to have another world?

116
00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:32.950
<v Speaker 1>I don't know why you keep talking to me about this mother and another world and an afterlife.

117
00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:34.030
<v Speaker 1>There is no mother.

118
00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:36.110
<v Speaker 1>There is no world outside this womb.

119
00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:36.910
<v Speaker 1>You're crazy.

120
00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:38.830
<v Speaker 1>Okay show me.

121
00:11:39.390 --> 00:11:41.630
<v Speaker 1>Show me this world that you keep talking about.

122
00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:42.710
<v Speaker 1>Show it to me right now.

123
00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:43.550
<v Speaker 1>I want to see it.

124
00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:46.510
<v Speaker 1>Prove to me that there is another world.

125
00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:49.710
<v Speaker 1>Prove to me that there is actually a mother.

126
00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:56.430
<v Speaker 1>I'm not gonna believe you unless and until I see that world and until I see that mother.

127
00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:07.550
<v Speaker 1>And I say, I can't show it to you right now, but I promise when you transition out of this world, this womb, you'll see both of them.

128
00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:11.390
<v Speaker 1>Oh, so now I'm supposed to trust you.

129
00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:15.310
<v Speaker 1>I'm supposed to trust your belief system, your intellect?

130
00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:16.670
<v Speaker 1>What if you're wrong?

131
00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:21.710
<v Speaker 1>Now this is us with Allah in this world.

132
00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:30.670
<v Speaker 1>There are so many of us denying the existence of the mother living in the comforts of this womb, of this dunya.

133
00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:35.070
<v Speaker 1>So now,

134
00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:44.910
<v Speaker 1>I begin this logical path of explanation and I say, look, you have been given these eyes, but there is so little to see here.

135
00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:49.710
<v Speaker 1>You've been given these ears, but there's so little to hear.

136
00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:54.030
<v Speaker 1>You've been given taste buds, but there is so little to taste here.

137
00:12:54.350 --> 00:13:00.990
<v Speaker 1>You have a nose with this magnificent ability to smell, but there's not a single fragrance here.

138
00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:08.830
<v Speaker 1>You have arms, you have feet, you have all these amazing gifts, but you cannot benefit from them within this womb.

139
00:13:08.990 --> 00:13:09.950
<v Speaker 1>So think about it.

140
00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:23.950
<v Speaker 1>These are of no use to you inside this womb, which means there must be another world that is out there, a world where you will be able to use and benefit from these gifts.

141
00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:26.310
<v Speaker 1>Think about it.

142
00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:33.550
<v Speaker 1>Your only purpose in this womb, in this world, is to draw your sustenance from your mother and develop these organs.

143
00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:45.070
<v Speaker 1>In other words, you're here so that you can prepare them for the next world where you will actually be using them, where you will actually benefit from them.

144
00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:48.670
<v Speaker 1>But does the fetus understand that?

145
00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:49.550
<v Speaker 1>No.

146
00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:51.470
<v Speaker 1>It doesn't.

147
00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:56.990
<v Speaker 1>To the fetus, the concept of another world and the existence of a mother is just ridiculous.

148
00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:03.630
<v Speaker 1>Just as the concept of a God and an afterlife is absurd to so many of us.

149
00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:08.030
<v Speaker 1>So now what happens?

150
00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:17.230
<v Speaker 1>This fetus continues to live in its ignorance and its arrogance until the nine months complete.

151
00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:19.950
<v Speaker 1>Now what happens?

152
00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:22.590
<v Speaker 1>Contractions begin.

153
00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:25.710
<v Speaker 1>The fetus starts panicking.

154
00:14:25.950 --> 00:14:26.870
<v Speaker 1>What's going on here?

155
00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:27.510
<v Speaker 1>What's happening?

156
00:14:28.730 --> 00:14:30.810
<v Speaker 1>This is what was promised to you.

157
00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:33.450
<v Speaker 1>I told you this day would come.

158
00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.770
<v Speaker 1>I told you this world is temporary.

159
00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:50.970
<v Speaker 1>So now with those contractions, this beautiful world of the fetus, this magnificent world it was living happily and comfortably in, it starts crumbling around it.

160
00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.530
<v Speaker 1>It starts falling apart all around it.

161
00:14:55.210 --> 00:14:58.250
<v Speaker 1>Now, isn't that exactly the description of the Day of Judgment?

162
00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:05.610
<v Speaker 1>When the earth is shaken up with its earthquakes.

163
00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:11.370
<v Speaker 1>And the earth discharges its burden.

164
00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:17.650
<v Speaker 1>And man says, What is wrong with this world?

165
00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:18.890
<v Speaker 1>What is wrong with this earth?

166
00:15:20.010 --> 00:15:24.690
<v Speaker 1>Yaw ma izin tuhaddisu akhbaraha bi anna rabbaka o haalaha

167
00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:30.330
<v Speaker 1>On this day, it will report the news of which your master has commanded it.

168
00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:35.930
<v Speaker 1>Yauma izin, yasduru naasu ashtatan liyurao a'malahum.

169
00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:41.930
<v Speaker 1>On this day, people will separate out, and they will be shown the results of their deeds.

170
00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:45.370
<v Speaker 1>Fa man yaamal misqala zarratin khairan yara.

171
00:15:45.770 --> 00:15:48.410
<v Speaker 1>So, whoever did an atom's weight of good will see it.

172
00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:51.850
<v Speaker 1>Wa man yaamal misqala zarratin sharran yara.

173
00:15:52.890 --> 00:16:19.690
<v Speaker 1>and whoever did an Adam's weight of evil will see it so the world of the fetus now comes to an end and it is forced out of it it is pushed out of it against its will you see does the fetus have a choice in whether it wants to stay in the womb or not no whether it wants to or not whether it's ready or not once its time is up that's it

174
00:16:20.650 --> 00:16:22.370
<v Speaker 1>It is pushed out into the next world.

175
00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:28.730
<v Speaker 1>It dies in the womb in order to be born again in the next world, you see.

176
00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:34.530
<v Speaker 1>Its death in the womb results in its creation in this world.

177
00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:37.530
<v Speaker 1>That's what the word intaqal means.

178
00:16:38.090 --> 00:16:41.530
<v Speaker 1>It comes from naqala, which means a transference.

179
00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:45.530
<v Speaker 1>It also means a copy or a replica.

180
00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:49.050
<v Speaker 1>That's what naqala means, a copy or a replica.

181
00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:49.690
<v Speaker 1>Why?

182
00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:57.450
<v Speaker 1>Because the next world is going to be a copy, it is going to be a replica of the first.

183
00:17:00.090 --> 00:17:05.770
<v Speaker 1>If you did good in the world, in this world, you will find good in the next world.

184
00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:10.090
<v Speaker 1>If you did evil in this world, you will find evil in the next world.

185
00:17:11.290 --> 00:17:13.770
<v Speaker 1>It's going to be a replica, it's going to be a copy.

186
00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:28.170
<v Speaker 1>If the fetus has not properly developed its eyes, its ears, its brain, its limbs in the womb of its mother, it is going to suffer the consequences of that in the afterlife of this dunya.

187
00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:30.730
<v Speaker 1>SubhanAllah.

188
00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:42.330
<v Speaker 1>So now this temporal world of the fetus is destroyed and it comes into this huge world that he was informed about.

189
00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:46.010
<v Speaker 1>this world that was promised to him in the womb.

190
00:17:48.890 --> 00:17:55.050
<v Speaker 1>He is now forced into this world, this afterlife that he chose not to believe in.

191
00:17:55.290 --> 00:18:00.970
<v Speaker 1>And then, as soon as it's out of the womb, who is the baby handed to?

192
00:18:02.650 --> 00:18:03.370
<v Speaker 1>The mother.

193
00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:05.290
<v Speaker 1>Subhanallah.

194
00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:11.450
<v Speaker 1>The mother that he said did not exist, the mother he denied his entire life in the womb.

195
00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:22.730
<v Speaker 1>So you can see that the fetus goes through the exact same confusion of the seen and the unseen while it's in the womb of its mother.

196
00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:26.010
<v Speaker 1>That's so many of us go through in this life.

197
00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:39.530
<v Speaker 1>The fetus that accepts the rububiya of its mother through the womb comes out fully developed and is now capable of enjoying all the benefits

198
00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:45.450
<v Speaker 1>that the afterlife has to offer, which is this physical world for the fetus.

199
00:18:46.090 --> 00:19:03.370
<v Speaker 1>But the fetus that rejected the rububia of the womb, it comes out underdeveloped, blind, deaf, mute, physically challenged, mentally challenged, incapable of benefiting from the joys and pleasures that this world has to offer.

200
00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:09.370
<v Speaker 1>We are all going through this exact same process in life.

201
00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:11.050
<v Speaker 1>Why?

202
00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:17.450
<v Speaker 1>Because Ad-Dunya Rahmul Akhra this world is the womb for the afterlife.

203
00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:31.690
<v Speaker 1>And here we have our Rab telling us, look, follow the Sharia, keep yourself clean, keep yourself pure, do your Salat, complete your fast, pay your Zakat, fulfill your obligations of Hajj.

204
00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:32.970
<v Speaker 1>And what do we say?

205
00:19:33.050 --> 00:19:33.450
<v Speaker 1>Why?

206
00:19:34.490 --> 00:19:35.850
<v Speaker 1>How is this going to help me?

207
00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.290
<v Speaker 1>It's not going to help you here.

208
00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:42.570
<v Speaker 1>That's not the purpose.

209
00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:46.250
<v Speaker 1>The obligations of Sharia is not meant for this world.

210
00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:50.930
<v Speaker 1>It's the sustenance for the development of our spiritual limbs.

211
00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:52.170
<v Speaker 1>That's what Sharia is.

212
00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:53.930
<v Speaker 1>It's a means like the womb.

213
00:19:56.810 --> 00:19:57.610
<v Speaker 1>It's a tool.

214
00:19:57.610 --> 00:20:08.810
<v Speaker 1>It's a mechanism, a means, an intermediary for the development of our spiritual limbs, for the development of our spiritual organs that are going to help us live a good life

215
00:20:09.610 --> 00:20:16.010
<v Speaker 1>After this world is over, that is where we will benefit from these fully developed spiritual organs.

216
00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:25.930
<v Speaker 1>In the afterlife, all we're doing here in this Dunya is developing them in order to use them in the next world, which is Jannah.

217
00:20:27.130 --> 00:20:28.410
<v Speaker 1>But how do you develop them?

218
00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:29.370
<v Speaker 1>Through the Shariah.

219
00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:37.450
<v Speaker 1>Because Jannah is described as a world that is incredibly beautiful, a world that is governed by a Rab.

220
00:20:38.890 --> 00:20:42.570
<v Speaker 1>who is intensely merciful, who is constantly merciful.

221
00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:52.570
<v Speaker 1>The Sharia is the umbilical cord providing the sustenance for the development of our spiritual existence, of our spiritual being.

222
00:20:54.410 --> 00:21:03.690
<v Speaker 1>Now whether we believe in it or not, whether we want to or not, whether we execute it or not, that next world is inevitable.

223
00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:04.970
<v Speaker 1>It's coming.

224
00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:07.210
<v Speaker 1>Right?

225
00:21:07.210 --> 00:21:12.730
<v Speaker 1>Al Jannatahaqun, Wannarahaqun, Wal Mautahaqun, Wal Barasahaqun, Wal Mizanahaqun, Wa Saratahaqun.

226
00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:15.170
<v Speaker 1>Paradise is a reality.

227
00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:16.650
<v Speaker 1>Hellfire is a reality.

228
00:21:16.890 --> 00:21:18.090
<v Speaker 1>Death is a reality.

229
00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:21.130
<v Speaker 1>Rising from graves is a reality.

230
00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:26.410
<v Speaker 1>The scales in which our actions will be weighed, that is a reality.

231
00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:28.410
<v Speaker 1>The straight path is a reality.

232
00:21:30.170 --> 00:21:32.770
<v Speaker 1>Wa annasaata atiyatun laraibafiha.

233
00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:35.210
<v Speaker 1>And that appointed moment, it is coming.

234
00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:37.370
<v Speaker 1>There is absolutely no doubt about it.

235
00:21:40.250 --> 00:21:44.330
<v Speaker 1>That is the world in which justice will be exacted.

236
00:21:46.010 --> 00:21:50.410
<v Speaker 1>Every incident for which you said, where is justice?

237
00:21:51.290 --> 00:21:53.210
<v Speaker 1>On that day we will see justice.

238
00:21:54.330 --> 00:22:04.170
<v Speaker 1>The innocent people that suffered momentarily in this short span of life, this dunya, this world, their momentary suffering

239
00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:24.890
<v Speaker 1>will be balanced out with never-ending gifts and pleasures in the afterlife and the one who caused those sufferings for fleeting gains and pleasures their pleasures will be counterbalanced with grievous pain and everlasting torment but that day of judgment is coming

240
00:22:30.650 --> 00:22:56.250
<v Speaker 1>these are all descriptions of the day of judgment when this universe will be destroyed this this world that we are so comfortable in it's going to end that day is coming when souls will be paired together when you will finally meet those loved ones

241
00:22:56.690 --> 00:23:25.970
<v Speaker 1>who left you behind in this world and when that little girl who was buried alive will be asked for what sin were you killed this is the day where Allah will exact justice this is the day of justice not this world not this dunya that we're living in that day all the deeds will open up

242
00:23:26.570 --> 00:23:52.090
<v Speaker 1>And when the book of deeds will be made public, wa iza samaa ukushitaat And when the sky will be stripped away, wa izal jaheem usoa'irat And when that hellfire is set ablaze, wa izal jannatu uslifaat And when the paradise is brought near, alimat nafsun ma ahdarat Every soul will know what it has brought with it.

243
00:23:53.530 --> 00:23:58.250
<v Speaker 1>All good will be rewarded on that day and all bad will be punished on that day.

244
00:23:59.650 --> 00:24:00.330
<v Speaker 1>Allahu Akbar.

245
00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:15.690
<v Speaker 1>And the fact of the matter is that we have such a benevolent, such a merciful, such a loving master who is just dying to reward us for the smallest good deed that we do in this world.

246
00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:20.090
<v Speaker 1>You know, it has been narrated by the Prophet that

247
00:24:20.970 --> 00:24:28.090
<v Speaker 1>there will be a man on the day of judgment and all this man ever did was lend money to others.

248
00:24:28.410 --> 00:24:29.690
<v Speaker 1>He was a money lender.

249
00:24:30.250 --> 00:24:38.570
<v Speaker 1>And usually such people are black hearted people because of interest and they use that as a mechanism to gain worldly profit.

250
00:24:39.930 --> 00:24:48.650
<v Speaker 1>But when this man sent out his servants to collect the money that people owed him, if the person was having a hard time returning back that money,

251
00:24:50.170 --> 00:24:54.250
<v Speaker 1>If that's what the servant would return and tell him, he would say, forget about it.

252
00:24:55.690 --> 00:25:07.530
<v Speaker 1>So on the day of judgment, this man comes before Allah and he does not have any good deeds to his name, except that he used to do that.

253
00:25:09.210 --> 00:25:17.370
<v Speaker 1>And Allah subhanahu wa ta'ala, He displays this man to everyone and He says, will I leave him to be more generous than me?

254
00:25:19.370 --> 00:25:22.250
<v Speaker 1>Will I leave this man to be more generous than me?

255
00:25:22.250 --> 00:25:22.890
<v Speaker 1>SubhanAllah.

256
00:25:23.210 --> 00:25:24.970
<v Speaker 1>He used to forgive people.

257
00:25:26.410 --> 00:25:28.650
<v Speaker 1>Do you think I am not going to forgive him today?

258
00:25:32.330 --> 00:25:39.210
<v Speaker 1>This is the master, the Rabb that we fail in our abudhiya towards.

259
00:25:43.210 --> 00:25:53.290
<v Speaker 1>On this day, every single good deed will be balanced with a reward from an immensely beneficent, from an incredibly loving and compassionate master.

260
00:25:53.930 --> 00:25:57.930
<v Speaker 1>All our delusions of grandeur in this world, they will be gone.

261
00:25:58.250 --> 00:26:05.130
<v Speaker 1>On that day, the muflis and the ghani, the destitute and the affluent, they will be separated.

262
00:26:08.330 --> 00:26:12.730
<v Speaker 1>Rasulullah once asked his companions

263
00:26:13.370 --> 00:26:15.930
<v Speaker 1>He asked, you know, man al-muflis.

264
00:26:15.930 --> 00:26:16.970
<v Speaker 1>Who is the muflis?

265
00:26:16.970 --> 00:26:18.410
<v Speaker 1>Who is the destitute?

266
00:26:19.770 --> 00:26:24.410
<v Speaker 1>They said, al-muflisu manla dinaru wala darhamu hindana ya Rasulullah.

267
00:26:25.530 --> 00:26:29.850
<v Speaker 1>The destitute is the one who does not have any darham or dinar to his name.

268
00:26:30.090 --> 00:26:31.290
<v Speaker 1>And the Prophet said, no.

269
00:26:32.810 --> 00:26:37.050
<v Speaker 1>He said, the greatest destitute of my Ummah on the Day of Judgment.

270
00:26:43.570 --> 00:27:09.530
<v Speaker 1>the greatest destitute of my Ummah on the Day of Judgment will be the one who comes with all of his prayers and all of his fasting and all of his Zakat wa ya'ti qat shata mahada wa qudifa haada wa akalamalaha haada wa safaqaddam mahada wa daraba haada but in addition to all of these good deeds he cheated this one

271
00:27:09.930 --> 00:27:16.810
<v Speaker 1>he lied to this one, he usurped the wealth of this one, he spilled the blood of this one, he struck this one.

272
00:27:19.850 --> 00:27:30.410
<v Speaker 1>And so his good deeds will be taken from his account and put into the account of this one and this one and this one.

273
00:27:31.970 --> 00:27:38.010
<v Speaker 1>And when his good deeds run out,

274
00:27:38.690 --> 00:28:07.450
<v Speaker 1>before justice is fully served the sins and falls of the remaining victims they will be taken from their accounts and added to his accounts and so despite living an entire life full of worship full of prayers full of fasting paying zakat because of his injustices that he committed with other people

275
00:28:08.010 --> 00:28:12.290
<v Speaker 1>because of the hurt that he caused to other people in this world.

276
00:28:12.570 --> 00:28:23.850
<v Speaker 1>This man will have to give up all his good deeds and he will have to take on all the horrible sins of his victims and he will finally be thrown into Hellfire.

277
00:28:24.170 --> 00:28:30.090
<v Speaker 1>This person, he said, will be the greatest destitute of my Ummah.

278
00:28:30.890 --> 00:28:35.290
<v Speaker 1>May Allah protect us all from being among these destitutes on the Day of Judgment.

279
00:28:36.330 --> 00:28:50.410
<v Speaker 1>Wahruddawan an alhamdulillahi rabbil alameen wassalatu wassalamu ala rasuli he saidina Muhammadin khatimin nabiin wassaidul Musaleen wala akhi wa wassi alibnabi talib aashrafil wassayeen walil aimatimin zoriatima taibinatahirin wassalam alayhi majmain al-fatah.
